You are working on Bios, an Android app (Kotlin + Jetpack Compose) that measures, compares each metric with the owner's own usual range, and shows the result. It never says what a measurement means. It is not a medical device.

Key constraints:
- All processing happens on-device. Bios has no server. Never add code that sends readings anywhere.
- No named condition, cause, advice or score against an outside reference in any text Bios shows. VocabularyGateTest enforces this; see docs/specs/instrument-only.md.
- AES-256 encryption at rest via SQLCipher.
- Max 500 lines per file. Split before adding to files near the limit.
- One logical change per prompt. Don't refactor unrelated code.

Architecture (android/app/src/main/java/com/bios/app/):
- model/ — Room entities and enums
- data/ and data/dao/ — databases, migrations, repositories, DAOs
- engine/ — baselines, the deviation score, statistics, sleep and cycle derivations, camera PPG signal processing
- ingest/ — source adapters (Health Connect, Gadgetbridge, sensors, vendor APIs), deduplication, sync worker
- alerts/ — the one deviation alert, its wording, notifications, source-disconnect notices
- export/ — JSON, CSV, FHIR and PDF export, FHIR import
- labocr/ — on-device OCR of lab reports
- provider/ — BiosHealthProvider for companion apps
- platform/ — LETHE integration, wipe, loopback API
- sync/ — device-to-device sync (off unless enabled)
- ui/ — Compose screens, components, theme
- android/bios-contracts — metric keys and the provider contract companions compile against

Patterns to follow:
- Use suspend functions and Flow for async
- Room DAOs return Flow<List<T>> for observable queries
- Business logic in engine/, not in UI or data layers
- Follow existing naming: PascalCase classes, camelCase functions

Before committing, run: ./scripts/code-quality-check.sh
